# Trivy ignore file for known false positives or accepted risks
# Format: CVE ID per line, with optional comment
#
# Add entries here when a vulnerability:
# - Is a false positive for our usage
# - Has no available fix yet and is accepted risk
# - Only affects dev dependencies not shipped to production
#
# Every entry needs a date, the reason, and the matching pnpm audit
# ignore (root package.json -> pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas) when the
# advisory also fails `pnpm audit --prod --audit-level=high`.
# Re-check each entry whenever the package publishes a new version.

# node-forge <=1.4.0, GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv (2026-10-23, WP-46).
# No fixed release exists (1.4.0 is the latest). The flaw is in RSA
# PKCS#1 v1.5 signature VERIFICATION (rsa publicKey.verify, and the
# certificate/chain verify helpers built on it): it accepts extra nested
# DigestAlgorithm elements. The API only uses node-forge to BUILD and
# PARSE CMS/ASN.1 (apps/api/src/sealing: kms-cms-signer, p12-tsa-signer,
# pades-signer, dss-injector, cert-chain-extractor, tsa-client,
# revocation-fetcher) and to sign with @signpdf/signer-p12. Nothing under
# apps/api/src calls publicKey.verify, certificate.verify or
# verifyCertificateChain, so the vulnerable path is unreachable at runtime.
# The only verify call is apps/api/scripts/verify-pades.ts, a CI checker
# that runs over PDFs the pipeline itself just sealed, not over untrusted
# input. Mirrored in pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas.
CVE-2026-85393
